<title>SWEDEN: Swedish forestry rallies on U.S. price hike talk.</title>
<headline>Swedish forestry rallies on U.S. price hike talk.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry sector shares rose on Wednesday amid rumours that U.S. producers had raised pulp prices, brokers said.</p>
<p>The forestry index on the Stockholm bourse was 1.21 percent higher at 1240 GMT while the general index was 0.28 percent higher.</p>
<p>Stora rose four crowns to 119 crowns while MoDo was five crowns up at 246. AssiDoman edged up 0.5 to 218 crowns.</p>
<p>&quot;As far as I know there are three big companies that have said they will lift prices from $580 a tonne to $630 -- Weyerhaeuser, Stone Container and Georgia Pacific,&quot; Anders Jansson, sales manager at Rottneros told Reuters.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
